Package: kitsPreview
Title: Teaching Wrappers Around 'dexter', 'immer' and 'cNORM' for the KIT Developmental Scale
Version: 0.25.0
Authors@R: person("Jie-Wen", "Tsai", email = "tsai.jiewen@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Thin, teaching-oriented wrappers that show how each step of the
    developmental scale of KIT (Kids in Taiwan: National Longitudinal Study of
    Child Development and Care) is done directly with 'dexter', 'immer' and
    'cNORM', and that check the numbers of the main package 'kits' (written in
    'RTMB'). The functions have the same names, main arguments and printout
    as 'kits', but their results have their own class names, so loading both
    packages changes no method of 'kits'. The items are calibrated with the
    partial credit model (Masters, 1982) <doi:10.1007/BF02296272> by
    conditional maximum likelihood, in 'dexter' (the default) or 'immer'.
    Both engines return the same table of step parameters on the same origin,
    keep the package's own result, and write the few lines of the package's
    own code that they ran. Cohorts are linked by mean/sigma (Marco, 1977)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1745-3984.1977.tb00033.x> on the Thurstonian thresholds of
    all steps, and domains with anchor items are linked to the D score of the
    Global Scales for Early Development (Weber et al., 2019)
    <doi:10.1136/bmjgh-2019-001724>. Person scores are weighted likelihood
    estimates (Warm, 1989) <doi:10.1007/BF02294627>. Norms are continuous
    sinh-arcsinh norms (Jones and Pewsey, 2009) <doi:10.1093/biomet/asp053>
    fitted with 'cNORM' (Lenhard and Lenhard, 2021)
    <doi:10.1177/0013164420928457>. Item and person fit, the formulas of every
    step, and standalone code are provided.
